// Rule: [T1486] Aurora - SAP Encryptor Flags
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1486
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Campaign-specific hunt for the Windows encryptor name and compiled command line flags recovered from an Aurora affiliate.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for sap encryptor flags using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Aurora Windows encryptor execution with source-documented flags
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Telemetry prerequisite: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint -> DeviceProcessEvents
// Scope: campaign-specific artifact; a match requires investigation and is not proof of encryption.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "sap.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-percent"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "-scanners"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "-noparallel"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "-esxi"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "-allowfolders"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, FileName, FolderPath,
          ProcessCommandLine, SHA1, ProcessId, ProcessUniqueId,
          AccountName, AccountSid, InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
